hi there steve kaufman here again uh the  linguist on language blog  founder of link  and uh there seems to be a lot of  interest in this subject of testing and  language learning so i thought i would  do  another video here while the subject is  still fresh in my mind  and uh i've sort of gave it some more  thought you know one thing that we do  like to do as humans  uh in all fields of endeavor is we do  like to measure our achievements we we  do like to in a sense test ourselves  so  presumably language learning is no  exception  uh i mean if we play tennis we like to  see how well we do we compete against  other tennis players  in golf we keep score so  uh yeah we would like to keep score in  our language learning  so i kind of thought it through and i  suggest that there are  three types of language testing or  language measurement  that matter the first and the most  important  is how we measure our own achievements  and this is the most important for the  simple reason  that um  language learning is all about ourselves  i mean we learn the language primarily  for ourselves it's our own activity it's  something that we do for ourselves it's  quite different from  i think was reinecke who one of the one  of a frequent and very welcome commenter  at my blog  uh was saying well you know we have to  measure things like we have driving  tests  yeah we have driving tests because we  can't have people on the road who can't  drive  driving is not a subjective something  that you just do for your own personal  enjoyment type of activity driving is  something that gets you from a to b  and also it involves the other people on  the road if you can't drive if you don't  know the rules of the road uh you are a  menace  um  you know similarly we have to have tests  for  people who are electricians or plumbers  or engineers  uh airline pilots uh you know even in  the field of language uh people who are  interpreters we need to determine just  what their skill level is  but most people learn languages for  their own purposes so  it's less important to have  even if such a thing were possible to  have some kind of an objective test for  most people  however people do want to measure  so the first thing is  my best test is you know how well do i  understand what i'm listening to  how well can i read a book  how difficult a book can i read  how much trouble do i have expressing  myself  most of us are pretty good  at self-evaluating at length we have six  levels and as long as there's no  pressure as long as i'm not trying to  get a job or prove to someone that i  have a skill which maybe i don't quite  have if there's no such  other reason people are quite capable of  evaluating themselves on a scale of of  one to six for example  low be you know absolute beginner uh  advanced beginner  lower intermediate advanced intermediate  uh sort of  somewhat advanced and very advanced  let's say six levels most people can do  that  and even if they don't measure  themselves on that scale  they're constantly aware of of  how well they're doing  however some people are not satisfied  with that and some people like to  compare themselves  so you know at link we do have  a measurement of the number of words you  know  we measure every form of the word so  depending on the language that can end  up being a large number because in some  languages  were the you know that are very  inflected as we say the words can have  many different forms depending on  case or depending on gender or depending  on  you know tense and person and so forth  and so on  so that's a measurement  there are very simple tests uh called  closed tests closed  where you look at attack  text and certain words are blank  and  then you have to pick the right word so  that's a measurement of how if you  according to links statistics claim to  know ten thousand words whether in fact  you do know them  um  a relatively easy thing to do in fact we  intend to introduce it  when we eventually have the time  at link so those are  the number of ways in which you can test  yourself but the best way really is you  have a good sense yourself of how well  you're communicating  uh if anything people tend to  underestimate their abilities so that's  insofar as testing yourself  the next issue is how do we test a  student and people have commented on my  blog we need to know whether the kids  are learning well  here i think the most important thing is  to test  the activity level of the student  and again that's something we attempt to  do at link we try to measure how many  hours of listening how many  words of reading  how many words of writing  how many hours of speaking  even the number of as we call them links  how many words and phrases have you  saved to your database you have to be  reading in order to be saving those to a  database so there are a number of things  that you can do  whether you're at a a  community like link which is on the  internet where we have ways of measuring  certain things or in a classroom  how many books have the kids read what  stories have they listened to  if you're asking them to bring in their  favorite words and phrases which i  suggest as some as an activity for the  classroom then are they bringing in  these words and phrases  uh you can also discuss with them what  they have read or claim to have read and  claim to have listened to so there are  ways of measuring the amount of activity  that kids are into without actually  testing them it's not a comprehension  test on whether you understood the book  it's merely a discussion about the book  just to get some sense that that the  student has in fact read the book or  listened to the book  or you know if have to bring in lists of  words and phrases that they liked or  want to learn these are all indications  that they are active and so i think that  the the most important thing in in  measuring the learner  rather than the learner measuring  themselves  is to measure the degree to which  they're active how much time are they  spending with the language  uh  of course we have other ways of testing  their ability i mean at some point  although not for the first few years  they will write and you will correct the  writing uh you will speak if you're a  teacher you will have an opportunity to  speak to them or they will speak to  others so you have a number of more  informal ways of measuring  their familiarity and comfort level in  the language  but you needn't give them a an 8 out of  10 and mark them down on the use of the  subjunctive for example  finally  the issue is how do we  test or measure  the school or the teacher the person  who's supposed to be  teaching these kids  one of the justifications for  testing is that it's also a test  of how effective the school is  or the teacher or the program  well my comment here is that our schools  are full of tests and yet the ultimate  test is that a very high percentage of  kids graduate not being able to use the  language  that's a pretty strong condemnation of  the school now how if you introduced a  new  approach how would you measure its  effectiveness  i think that  judging how well someone uses the  language  is not so difficult  and if the net result is that  the student  is comfortable with their own  achievements in the language in other  words that first type of testing that i  talked about which is aimed at  self-evaluating  if  you have numbers that show that the  students are very active in the language  that is that second group measuring  their level activity level of activity  and if you have applied  a form of language education that is  based on letting kids choose what to  learn and what to listen to and what to  read rather than testing them on points  of grammar that have been taught  if all of these things have happened the  student is satisfied with their own  level you have uh a record of their  level of activity  and you are in fact teaching in a way  that  enables them to be success happy with  their performance and that they are  active if you're doing all these things  you've done it and then we don't need to  measure you because we know that the  system works if that makes sense anyway  thank you for listening bye for now
 

